      "category": "Pawn",
      "signature": "GetLastMovementInputVector(Target)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "APawn*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "FVector",
      "docs": "Return the last input vector in world space that was processed by ConsumeMovementInputVector(), which is usually done by the Pawn or PawnMovementComponent.\nAny user that needs to know about the input that last affected movement should use this function.\nFor example an animation update would want to use this, since by default the order of updates in a frame is:\nPlayerController (device input) -> MovementComponent -> Pawn -> Mesh (animations)\n@return The last input vector in world space that was processed by ConsumeMovementInputVector().\n@see AddMovementInput(), GetPendingMovementInputVector(), ConsumeMovementInputVector()"
    },
